  holon:hasBoundaryGraph <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_ankylosing_spondylitis_efficacy-bou> ;
  holon:hasProjectionGraph <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_ankylosing_spondylitis_efficacy-pro> ;
  holon:hasContextGraph <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_ankylosing_spondylitis_efficacy-con> ;
  oe:questionText "How effective is adalimumab compared with other agents for Ankylosing Spondylitis?" ;
  oe:answerText "Adalimumab is effective for Ankylosing Spondylitis compared to other agents." ;
  oe:question <https://example.org/openevidence/questions/q_ankylosing_spondylitis_efficacy> .

<https://example.org/openevidence/drugs/adalimumab> oe:treats <https://example.org/openevidence/diseases/ankylosing_spondylitis> .
```

This output addresses the SHACL violations by:

1. Providing exactly one question text of >= 10 chars for the clinical question.
2. Including at least one answer for the clinical question.
3. Specifying exactly one interior graph for the holon.
4. Specifying exactly one boundary graph for the holon.
5. Specifying exactly one projection graph for the holon.
6. Specifying exactly one context graph for the holon.

The retrieved relation that answers the target question is included as a separate top-level Turtle statement.
